WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.350 align:start position:0%
 
hi everyone  it's been 10 years in the making but  george r.r martin has made progress on  winds of winter  even if that progress has been slowed up  by his other projects  here's the latest update  martin has updated fans on his blog  about progress on various things he's  working on which includes winds of  winter the penultimate book in the  songs of ice and fire series  unfortunately the update doesn't give a  release date but reassured fans that the  book is being worked on  the author joked about the fact that he  hadn't been working on the railroad  despite an ongoing project to open a  restored 19th century railway called sky  railway in martin's home state of new  mexico which will run between santa fe  and lammy  instead he wrote that he's been working  on the massively anticipated book which  will be his first in the acclaimed  series since a game of thrones first  aired on hbo in 2011.  martin purchased the railway in 2020  with a group of business partners  on top of his railway martin also  revealed other projects that made  writing the book more challenging  he revealed that he's a prolific  executive producer on shows like dark  wins for amc joker town for peacock and  who fears death for hbo amongst others  it's clear that the various meetings for  these shows are taking up a lot of his  time  there have been hints by the author in  other blog posts that he may help write  some episodes for the upcoming game of  thrones prequel house of the dragon  which is based on martin's fire and  blood  if he does then expect even more delays  on winds of winter  while this book remains george r.r  martin's current literary project he's  already made plans to pen several other  stories in the future  a fourth dunk and eggs short story will  follow before martin completes the a  song of ice and fire series  he'll sandwich that with a fifth dunkin  egg story before moving on to fire and  blood volume 2.  clearly all this planning has also  interfered with progress on his current  work but it appears as though movement  is there with the book we're all waiting  for and a release date is just around  the corner

